# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Ablation caches are NOT IGNORED — one per deck is tracked under
# results/caches/, each with the fingerprint it was BUILT at recorded in
# results/caches/PROVENANCE.json (stamped by ablation.py, never rewritten).
# See KNOWN_ISSUES.md 0z23 and docs/ABLATION_CACHES.md, which is generated.
#
# They are tracked so a clone can reproduce or extend the tables without the
# run, which is about four hours for six decks. The cost is that a stale cache
# arrives with a checkout; the guard is provenance, not deletion -- a cache
# whose built-at fingerprint differs from live is SUSPECT until
# check_unchanged_decks shows its baseline did not move, and check_docs fails
# on a SUSPECT or UNRECORDED cache. That safety net was once not maintained
# (ten caches deleted in b09055c with the generator left describing them),
# which is why check_docs now verifies the generated manifest too.
#
# If you produce a cache worth keeping, commit it together with its stamped
# provenance and a regenerated manifest — an untracked cache with no
# provenance is the thing this comment exists to prevent.
#
# The blank mode is IN THE FILENAME on purpose: a cache measured against a
# different blank is not resumable onto, and a suffix nothing reads is how the
# N-in-the-key bug happened the first time.

# Spreadsheet lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Everything below moved under results/ in the 2026-09-09 reorganisation. The
# patterns are anchored there rather than left bare, so a stray ablation_*.log
# written into the root by a script run the wrong way is VISIBLE in git status
# instead of silently ignored.

# Ablation stderr progress logs — noise, the .txt tables are the artefact
results/ablation_*.log

# Regeneration scratch — the finished .txt tables ARE tracked
results/ablation_*.txt.new
results/regen.log

# A void table kept only long enough to diff against; not an artefact.
results/ablation_*_VOID_*.txt

# tutor_policy.py's scratch log
results/tutor_log.json

# check_unchanged_decks.py's baseline dumps
results/baselines*.json

# run_karlov_boots.py / run_azusa_slot.py progress marker, written by the
# shell that chains them so a wait loop can tell a finished run from a
# crashed one. Not a result.
results/.slot_progress
results/.fra_progress
results/.b2_progress
results/.fix_progress

# run_karlov_fra.py / run_azusa_fra.py stage markers, written by the shell that
# chains them. Not a result.
results/.fra_progress
